---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
import { safetyResources } from '../data/safety-resources';

// docs/03-feature-spec.md §16.
const design = [
  { icon: 'scale', title: 'Identical powers', text: 'Both partners can do exactly the same things. There is no admin role, and no setting gives one person authority over the other.' },
  { icon: 'door-open', title: 'Unpair instantly, on your own', text: 'Either partner can unpair at any time from Settings with one confirmation. The other person is not asked and cannot stop it.' },
  { icon: 'eye-off', title: 'No watching', text: 'The app shares no location, no list of apps, no messages, no browsing and no Screen Time usage. Partners see only minutes, requests, challenges, kudos and the shared streak.' },
  { icon: 'life-buoy', title: 'Emergency unlock, always', text: 'Fifteen minutes with no approval, even with zero minutes and even without a partner. Phone calls, Messages and Maps are best left out of protected time entirely.' },
  { icon: 'smartphone', title: 'Your phone, your choices', text: 'Each person chooses their own paused apps on their own phone and gives Apple’s Screen Time permission themselves. Nobody can set it up on your behalf from another device.' },
  { icon: 'sparkles', title: 'No punishment', text: 'Nothing is taken away and nobody is shamed. The only thing that can end is a streak, and a new one starts the same day.' },
];
---

<Base
  title="Safety by design"
  description={`How ${site.name} is designed so it cannot be used to control a partner, how to unpair on your own, and where to find relationship-safety support.`}
  og="safety"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Safety', path: '/safety/' }]}
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Safety by design</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        An app that pauses apps for couples has to be built so that it cannot become a tool for control. Here is how
        {site.name} is designed, and where to turn if something feels wrong.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="grid grid--3">
      {
        design.map((item) => (
          <div class="card item">
            <Icon name={item.icon} />
            <h2>{item.title}</h2>
            <p>{item.text}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>What a healthy use looks like</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} is for two people who both want more time together and choose it freely. It should feel like a
        shared project. You both set it up, you both can change it, and either of you can stop.
      </p>

      <h2>Signs something is not right</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You were pressured to install the app or to pair.</li>
        <li>You feel you cannot say no to a request, or cannot ask for time without an argument.</li>
        <li>Your partner insists on choosing your paused apps or your schedule for you.</li>
        <li>You are afraid of how your partner would react if you unpaired.</li>
        <li>The app is one of several ways your partner checks on you or limits who you talk to.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        None of that is what this app is for. You can leave it at any moment, and you do not owe anyone an explanation.
      </p>

      <h2>How to step away</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Unpair:</strong> in the app, open Settings, go to your partner and choose Unpair. It is immediate.</li>
        <li><strong>Turn off protected time:</strong> once unpaired, your schedule is yours alone to change or switch off.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Remove Screen Time access:</strong> in your iPhone's Settings, under Screen Time, you can remove the
          app's access at any time.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Delete your account:</strong> see the steps on our <a href="/support/#delete-account">support page</a>.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        When you unpair, your partner receives a short, neutral notification that the pairing ended. If that
        notification could put you at risk, please talk to one of the services below first. They can help you plan.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--sunken" id="resources">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>People who can help</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          If you are in immediate danger, call your local emergency number (911 in the United States). The services
          below are free and confidential.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid--2">
        {
          safetyResources.map((resource) => (
            <div class="card item">
              <h3>{resource.name}</h3>
              <p>{resource.description}</p>
              <ul class="contact">
                {resource.phone && (
                  <li>
                    <Icon name="phone" size={20} />
                    <a href={resource.phone.href}>{resource.phone.label}</a>
                  </li>
                )}
                {resource.text && (
                  <li>
                    <Icon name="message-circle" size={20} />
                    {resource.text}
                  </li>
                )}
                <li>
                  <Icon name="link" size={20} />
                  <a href={resource.url} rel="noopener noreferrer">{resource.urlLabel}</a>
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
      <p class="outside">
        Outside the United States, search for a domestic abuse helpline in your country, or ask a doctor or local
        support service. If someone may be checking your device, consider using a phone or computer they cannot access.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>Tell us</h2>
      <p>
        If any part of {site.name} feels controlling, or you see a way it could be misused, we want to hear about it:
        <a href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}?subject=Safety`}>{site.supportEmail}</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        {site.name} is a tool for spending time together. It is not a counseling service and cannot respond to
        emergencies.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .item {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    align-content: start;
  }
  .item h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0;
  }
  .item > :global(.icon) {
    color: var(--sage);
  }
  .contact {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .contact li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    min-height: 32px;
  }
  .outside {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
    max-width: 680px;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
</style>
